# Secrets / local env
.env

# Node
# No trailing slash on node_modules, deliberately: a trailing slash matches a
# DIRECTORY only, and CLAUDE.md tells you to symlink node_modules from another
# worktree rather than run `npm ci` (its postinstall clobbers the host's
# agent-browser). A symlink is not a directory, so `web/node_modules/` left the
# symlink untracked and one `git add -A` staged a link pointing outside the repo.
# The bare pattern matches file, dir and symlink alike; agent/ and the bare form
# are here because the same symlink trick is used for both other workspaces.
#
# The bare `node_modules` alone would cover all three -- a gitignore pattern with no
# slash matches at ANY depth, so `git check-ignore -v` attributes both specific paths
# to that last line rather than to the two above it. They are kept anyway: the two
# named workspaces are the ones this repo actually has, and a reader scanning for
# "is web/node_modules ignored?" should find the answer written down rather than have
# to know the any-depth rule. Redundant, not wrong.
web/node_modules
agent/node_modules
node_modules
web/dist/
# Rendered Homebrew formula output (task brew:formula); the template is Formula/uzi-cli.rb
/dist/

# Machine-local scratch dir, never committed (e.g. symlinks to reference checkouts
# kept outside the repo). No trailing slash, for the same reason node_modules above
# has none: a symlink is not a directory, so `inspiration/` would leave the links
# untracked-but-not-ignored and one `git add -A` would commit an absolute path off
# this machine into the repo.
inspiration

